  rules: [
    "1\uFE0F\u20E3 COMPLEX SENTENCES NIMA?\n\nComplex sentence — bosh gap (main clause) va bir yoki bir nechta tobe gapdan (subordinate clause) tashkil topgan gap. B2 darajasida murakkab fikrlarni ifodalash uchun zarur.\n\n\uD83D\uDCCC SUBORDINATION: Although it rained, we enjoyed the trip.\n\uD83D\uDCCC COORDINATION: I studied hard, so I passed the exam.\n\uD83D\uDCCC RELATIVE CLAUSE: The book that you gave me is fascinating.\n\uD83D\uDCCC NOUN CLAUSE: I think that we should leave now.\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Complex sentence = independent + dependent clause(s)\n\uD83D\uDD34 Compound sentence = two independent clauses joined by coordinator",
    "2\uFE0F\u20E3 SUBORDINATION — TOBE GAPLAR\n\nSubordinator (tobe bog'lovchi) — ikki gapni bog'lab, birini ikkinchisiga tobe qiladi:\n\nTIME: when, while, after, before, until, as soon as\n  When I arrived, they had already left.\n  She waited until he finished.\n\nREASON: because, since, as\n  He passed because he studied hard.\n  Since it's late, we should go home.\n\nCONCESSION: although, even though, though\n  Although it was cold, she went swimming.\n\nCONDITION: if, unless, provided that\n  If you study, you will pass.\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Subordinator + clause = subordinate clause\n\uD83D\uDD34 Subordinate clause must attach to a main clause",
    "3\uFE0F\u20E3 COORDINATION — TENG BOG'LOVCHILAR\n\nCoordinator (teng bog'lovchi) — ikki mustaqil gapni bog'laydi:\n\nAND: qo'shish\n  I went to the store and bought some milk.\n\nBUT: qarama-qarshilik\n  She is rich but she is not happy.\n\nOR: tanlov\n  You can stay here or you can come with us.\n\nSO: natija\n  He was tired, so he went to bed early.\n\nYET: qaramay\n  She worked hard, yet she failed.\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 FANBOYS: For, And, Nor, But, Or, Yet, So\n\uD83D\uDD34 Coordinator bilan comma ishlatiladi (ikki independent clause o'rtasida)",
    "4\uFE0F\u20E3 RELATIVE CLAUSES — SIFAT GAPLAR\n\nRelative clause — otni ta'riflovchi gap:\n\nDEFINING (ajralmas):\n  The man who lives next door is a doctor.\n  The book which I read was amazing.\n  The girl that I met is from Italy.\n\nNON-DEFINING (qo'shimcha, comma bilan):\n  My brother, who lives in London, is a lawyer.\n  The Eiffel Tower, which is in Paris, is beautiful.\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Defining = no commas (gap ma'nosi uchun muhim)\n\uD83D\uDD34 Non-defining = with commas (qo'shimcha ma'lumot)\n\uD83D\uDD34 Who = people, Which = things, That = people/things (defining only)",
    "5\uFE0F\u20E3 NOUN CLAUSES — OT GAPLAR\n\nNoun clause — gap ichida noun vazifasida keladi:\n\nTHAT CLAUSE:\n  I believe that he is telling the truth.\n  That he passed the exam surprised everyone.\n\nWH- CLAUSE:\n  I don't know what she wants.\n  Can you tell me where the station is?\n  The question is how we can solve this.\n\nWHETHER / IF CLAUSE:\n  I wonder whether he will come.\n  I'm not sure if this is correct.\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Noun clause can be subject, object, or complement\n\uD83D\uDD34 That is often optional: I know (that) he is right.",
    "6\uFE0F\u20E3 PUNCTUATION IN COMPLEX SENTENCES\n\nSubordinate clause boshida → comma:\n  Although it rained, we went out.\n  If you study, you will pass.\n\nSubordinate clause oxirida → NO comma:\n  We went out although it rained.\n  You will pass if you study.\n\nRelative clause (non-defining) → commas:\n  My father, who is 60, still works.\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Comma qoidasi: subordinate clause FIRST → comma\n\uD83D\uDD34 Subordinate clause LAST → no comma",
    "7\uFE0F\u20E3 O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n\u2022 Comma splice: ikki independent clause ni faqat comma bilan bog'lash\n  XATO: I came home, I made dinner.\n  TO'G'RI: I came home, and I made dinner.\n\n\u2022 Run-on sentence: ikki gapni bog'lovchisiz yozish\n  XATO: I love reading books I read every day.\n  TO'G'RI: I love reading books, and I read every day.\n\n\u2022 Who va which ni adashtirish:\n  XATO: The book who I read\n  TO'G'RI: The book which I read\n\n\u2022 That ni non-defining relative clause da ishlatish:\n  XATO: My brother, that lives in London\n  TO'G'RI: My brother, who lives in London\n\n\u2022 Subordinate clause ni mustaqil ishlatish (sentence fragment):\n  XATO: Although it rained.\n  TO'G'RI: Although it rained, we went out.",
  ],
