    passage: `Uzbekistan, which is one of Central Asia's most populous nations, has embarked on an ambitious transition to a green economy. Although the country possesses abundant fossil fuel resources, the government has recognised that renewable energy offers a more sustainable path forward. The Strategy for Transition to a Green Economy, which was adopted in 2019, sets targets that include reducing carbon emissions by 35% by 2030. Because the country receives over 300 sunny days per year, solar energy presents an opportunity that few other nations can match. However, significant investment in grid infrastructure is needed if these ambitious goals are to be achieved.`,
